`B=$(git merge-base HEAD "${MOE_LAND_TARGET:-HEAD}"); git diff --name-only "$B" -- . ':(exclude).moe'; git diff -U0 "$B" -- docs/MCP_SERVER.md | sed -n 's/^@@ -[0-9,]* +\([0-9]*\).*/\1/p' | while read -r s; do awk -v s="$s" '/^### /{h=$0} NR==s{print h; exit}' docs/MCP_SERVER.md; done | sort -u`

Expected output:
- the first command prints only docs/MCP_SERVER.md;
- the loop prints only `### moe.amend_plan_step` and `### moe.get_activity_log`.

Paste both into the completion summary (QA checks the same with `git show --stat <sha>`).

Then read both bullets against the code once more. Check each item:
- the introduced-only rule (`already` set vs `introduced`);
- the default-action text, verbatim from amendPlanStep.ts;
- the distinct-values and present-only-when-non-empty behaviour (getActivityLog.ts ~:145/:162);
- no claim that the code does not make, e.g. error.data contents.

Error handling: if a check fails, fix the text and re-run step 3's command as the fresh test evidence.
